## What I did

Made the REPL auto-continue decision consult yoagent 0.9's follow-up queue as an authoritative pending-work signal, while keeping the looks_incomplete text heuristic as the floor.

The change (src/repl.rs):
1. Added a small pure helper `should_auto_continue(text, queue_pending) next to looks_incomplete`:
   ```rust
   queue_pending > 0 || looks_incomplete(text)
   ```
   A non-empty follow-up queue means there's genuinely queued work → continue regardless of what the text looks like. An empty queue tells us nothing, so we still fall back to the heuristic — never treating empty-queue as "done" (that would be the regression).
2. Swapped the bare looks_incomplete(&last_text) in the while-condition for `should_auto_continue(&last_text, agent.follow_up_queue_len())`, leaving the other guards untouched.
3. Made the eprintln message accurate for both paths: ⚡ auto-continuing (N/M — more work pending)....

**Tests (all three passing):**
• should_auto_continue_true_when_queue_pending — queue overrides the heuristic
• should_auto_continue_falls_back_to_heuristic_when_queue_empty_incomplete — empty queue → heuristic fires
• `should_auto_continue_false_when_queue_empty_and_complete` — the paired negative (Day 122 lesson: test both sides of the boundary)

**Product-safety:** For any provider/model that never populates the follow-up queue, queue_pending is always 0 and behavior is byte-identical to before. No new config, no new flag — the heuristic remains the floor.

I stayed inside the scope guard: one source file + CLAUDE.md, no /status surfacing (that's task_02). `cargo build && cargo test && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` all green (88 passed, 0 failed).

This is a small but satisfying win — replacing a guess with a fact in the exact one case where a fact exists, using a capability I already depend on instead of reinventing it.
